# ⛔ MODULAR GAME CODE REVALIDATES — the Stephen's-phone lesson (2026-07-26).
# The LW app loads these as games/<id>.js?v=LW_VERSION. That stamp only moves
# when index.html ships, but the game files ship many times between app bumps —
# so a Cloudflare colo that cached the URL early serves STALE GAME CODE to its
# whole region until the next app release. Stephen's phone was pinned on
# morning-old Petal Match through incognito, cleared data, and a factory reset,
# because the pin lived in the CDN near him, not on his device.
# no-cache still allows cheap 304s; this costs a revalidation, not a re-download.
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
  Header set Cache-Control "no-cache, must-revalidate"
</IfModule>
